From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8750: never vote ACV from HLOS

Mainline gives the SM8750 ACV BCM an enable mask of BIT(0), so HLOS
asserts that ACV bit whenever it holds any DDR vote and drops it in the
sleep set. The vendor driver (sun.c) declares ACV as a mask-type BCM with
no enable mask, so HLOS always votes 0 there.

On the AYN Odin 3 that awake-to-asleep ACV transition hangs s2idle,
followed by a watchdog reset about 2.5 minutes later, whenever no other HLOS
DDR vote is held. A sleep-set vote to ebi avoids it (that is why the
PCIe suspend OPP floor works), a vote that stops at qns_llcc does not,
and AOSS-level prevent_ddr_collapse, a fixed DDR frequency and
prevent_aoss_sleep do not either.

Add a mask_type flag so a mask BCM with no enable mask is still voted,
as 0, and use it for the SM8750 ACV.
---
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
@@ -116,6 +116,8 @@
  * @vote_y: aggregated threshold values, represents peak_bw when @type is bw bcm
  * @vote_scale: scaling factor for vote_x and vote_y
  * @enable_mask: optional mask to send as vote instead of vote_x/vote_y
+ * @mask_type: aggregate as a bitmask even when @enable_mask is 0, so the
+ * BCM is still voted (as 0) instead of as bandwidth
  * @dirty: flag used to indicate whether the bcm needs to be committed
  * @keepalive: flag used to indicate whether a keepalive is required
  * @aux_data: auxiliary data used when calculating threshold values and
@@ -133,6 +135,7 @@
 	u64 vote_y[QCOM_ICC_NUM_BUCKETS];
 	u64 vote_scale;
 	u32 enable_mask;
+	bool mask_type;
 	bool dirty;
 	bool keepalive;
 	struct bcm_db aux_data;
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
@@ -286,7 +286,7 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&voter->lock);
 	list_for_each_entry(bcm, &voter->commit_list, list) {
-		if (bcm->enable_mask)
+		if (bcm->enable_mask || bcm->mask_type)
 			bcm_aggregate_mask(bcm);
 		else
 			bcm_aggregate(bcm);
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
@@ -1021,9 +1021,14 @@
 	.link_nodes = { &qnm_snoc_sf },
 };
 
+/*
+ * The vendor driver never sets an ACV bit from HLOS (mask type, no enable
+ * mask). Asserting BIT(0) while awake and dropping it in the sleep set hangs
+ * s2idle on SM8750 whenever no other HLOS DDR vote is held.
+ */
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_acv = {
 	.name = "ACV",
-	.enable_mask = BIT(0),
+	.mask_type = true,
 	.num_nodes = 1,
 	.nodes = { &ebi },
 };
